@page
@model FirewallModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Firewall";

    var panelUrl = Url.Page("Firewall", "Panel");
}

<div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-3">
    <h1 class="h3 mb-0">Firewall</h1>
</div>

<p class="text-secondary">
    The packet filter on this machine, applied by the Helper — the one process here that runs as
    root (D142). What the firewall allows is derived from what this system is configured to listen
    on, so it is shown rather than edited: change a SIP port on the
    <a asp-page="/Settings/Sip">SIP settings</a> page and the expected ruleset below changes with it.
</p>

<p class="text-secondary">
    Four rules are always in force and are not listed here, because nothing this page sends can
    add or remove them: loopback, established connections, ICMP, and SSH on port 22 (D143). The
    Helper writes those itself, which is what makes it impossible to lock this machine out with
    the button below. fail2ban's bans live in a table of their own and are left alone.
</p>

@* The panel arrives from the Panel handler, and comes back after every apply. *@
<div id="firewall" hx-get="@panelUrl" hx-trigger="load">
    <p class="text-secondary">Asking the helper…</p>
</div>
